NOTICE

This skill (mcpe-native-modding) teaches the methodology of several
open-source projects, one per language/runtime combination:

- **C++ / preloader runtime** — BedrockTools
  (https://github.com/RadiantByte/BedrockTools)
- **C++ / BreezeAPI runtime** — BreezeAPI
  (https://github.com/wisebreeze/BreezeAPI), Apache-2.0
- **Rust** — mtbinloader2
  (https://github.com/mcbegamerxx954/mtbinloader2)

The hook/patch/signature/build patterns for each path are derived from
the corresponding project's code and documentation. This skill is
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see the repository root
LICENSE).

Referenced upstream projects:

- BedrockTools (https://github.com/RadiantByte/BedrockTools) — C++
  methodology source for the preloader runtime.
- preloader-android (https://github.com/LiteLDev/preloader-android) — the
  preloader SDK.
- LeviLaunchroid (https://github.com/LiteLDev/LeviLaunchroid) — the
  launcher for the preloader runtime.
- BreezeAPI (https://github.com/wisebreeze/BreezeAPI) — the Dobby-based
  C++ runtime with QuickJS.
- Dobby (https://github.com/jmpews/Dobby) — inline hook engine used by
  BreezeAPI.
- QuickJS (https://bellard.org/quickjs/) — JavaScript engine embedded in
  BreezeAPI.
- mtbinloader2 (https://github.com/mcbegamerxx954/mtbinloader2) — Rust
  methodology source (bhook, plt-rs, tinypatscan, region, ctor).
- bhook (https://github.com/mcbegamerxx954/bhook) — Rust inline hook
  crate used by mtbinloader2.
- plt-rs, tinypatscan, region, ctor — Rust crates referenced by the
  Rust path.

Use responsibly: hook/patch only binaries you are authorized to modify,
keep work to learning/personal use, and respect the game's terms of
service.

